1
00:00:00,464 --> 00:00:02,094
[TOILET FLUSHES]

2
00:00:03,342 --> 00:00:05,302
(Leonard:)He offered to send you
to the North Pole?

3
00:00:05,469 --> 00:00:08,139
(Leonard:)Yes.
In fact, he was quite enthusiastic.

4
00:00:08,639 --> 00:00:12,099
He said, "Frankly,
if I could send you tonight, I would."

5
00:00:13,936 --> 00:00:15,976
Okay. Well, do you wanna go?

6
00:00:16,147 --> 00:00:18,897
(Sheldon:)Of course not.
I'm a theoretical physicist.

7
00:00:19,066 --> 00:00:22,946
(Sheldon:)A career I chose in no small part
because it's indoors.

8
00:00:23,529 --> 00:00:27,069
(Sheldon:)But if I'm able to detect slow-moving
magnetic monopoles there...

9
00:00:27,241 --> 00:00:29,911
(Sheldon:)...I will be the scientist
who confirmed string theory.

10
00:00:30,077 --> 00:00:31,997
And people will write books about me.

11
00:00:32,163 --> 00:00:37,413
Third graders will create macaroni-art
dioramas depicting scenes from my life.

12
00:00:38,002 --> 00:00:42,092
(Leonard:)Sure. Maybe a tableau of me
trying to pummel you to death.

13
00:00:42,882 --> 00:00:44,592
(Sheldon:)Sarcasm?

14
00:00:44,759 --> 00:00:46,469
(Leonard:)Maybe.

15
00:00:47,345 --> 00:00:49,425
I am on the horns of a dilemma.

16
00:00:49,597 --> 00:00:53,597
(Sheldon:)Can you imagine me, Sheldon Cooper,
at the North Pole?

17
00:00:53,768 --> 00:00:55,728
(Leonard:)Easy peasy. I'm doing it right now.

18
00:00:56,979 --> 00:00:59,019
(Sheldon:)I'm not good with cold, Leonard.

